To: BLISS Logan * OPRD <Logan.BLISS@oprd.oregon.gov>
Subject: Re: Question

Hey, can you tell me who opens the gate on my days off? They didn't open it=
 this morning. I'll take care of it. Can you let me address it with them so=
 they don't feel called out? Thanks.

________________________________
From: Robert Samuel White
Sent: Wednesday, February 19, 2025 6:53:17 AM
To: BLISS Logan * OPRD <Logan.BLISS@oprd.oregon.gov<mailto:Logan.BLISS@oprd=
.oregon.gov>>
Subject: Question

Good morning, Logan.

I hate that I have to ask you this, because it feels like I'm breaking a co=
mmitment I made to you, and I appreciated the accommodation you made for me=
 to stay at this particular site, but I have to ask.

Can you find someone else to lock the gate at night? I'm not getting enough=
 sleep. I thought I could do it, but it doesn't match my natural patterns, =
so I've been sleeping far less than I should be.

And I just want to say I appreciated yesterday a lot and I hope you won't b=
e a stranger. I think you might have noticed I'm a little off right now. I =
am dealing with some pretty heavy things right now and I haven't processed =
it all. Hopefully I'll be back to my old self soon.

Now I'm going to go enjoy my "weekend." Take care.

Sam

